### AML case workflow (FR-AML-2, FR-AML-4, M9, ADR 0007), risk-aml-service on port 8081. COMPLIANCE_OFFICER only.
# Fake test data only. aml-demo.http is the story (structuring -> freeze -> escalate -> STR); this file has the other
# branch, closing a false positive, and the filters.
# Prerequisites: "officer1: token" and "customer1: token" in auth.http (officer1 needs a fresh TOTP code:
#   scripts/aml-demo-webhooks.sh totp), and at least one OPEN case (any rule hit, e.g. the AML demo or a k6 run).
# Workflow: OPEN -> INVESTIGATING (assign) -> CLOSED_FALSE_POSITIVE (close) or ESCALATED (escalate). Anything else is
# 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION; only the assigned officer may finish a case (409 NOT_CASE_ASSIGNEE).

### officer1: all cases, oldest first (a queue) -> 200 {content:[{id, walletId, status, highestSeverity, ...}], page, size, ...}
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1: open cases only (status: OPEN, INVESTIGATING, CLOSED_FALSE_POSITIVE, ESCALATED; walletId also filters)
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases?status=OPEN&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

> {% if (response.body.content.length > 0) client.global.set("fp_case_id", response.body.content[0].id); %}

### officer1: the case with its alerts, freeze requests and transaction facts
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### Closing an OPEN case without taking it first -> 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"resolution": "FALSE_POSITIVE", "notes": "Salary and rent, documented by the customer."}

### officer1: assign to self (empty body; {"assigneeId": "..."} reassigns) -> 200 INVESTIGATING
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Notes are required -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"resolution": "FALSE_POSITIVE", "notes": ""}

### officer1: close as a false positive -> 200 CLOSED_FALSE_POSITIVE
# This does NOT unfreeze the wallet: that stays a separate officer action in core-app
# (POST /api/v1/compliance/wallets/{id}/unfreeze, wallet.http), with its own reason and audit row.
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"resolution": "FALSE_POSITIVE", "notes": "Salary and rent, documented by the customer."}

### Escalating a closed case -> 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/escalate
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"notes": "Too late: the case is closed."}

### A closed case has no STR report -> 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION (aml-demo.http step 16 shows a real one)
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/str-report
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### A customer on the AML API -> 403
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### officer1: every alert, newest first (FR-AML-2) -> 200 {content:[{id, caseId, walletId, ruleCode, severity, details, createdAt}], page, size, ...}
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/alerts?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

> {% if (response.body.content.length > 0) client.global.set("alert_wallet_id", response.body.content[0].walletId); %}

### officer1: alerts by rule and severity (ruleCode R1-R4; severity MEDIUM or HIGH) -> 200
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/alerts?ruleCode=R2&severity=HIGH
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1: one wallet's alerts (from the first request) -> 200
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/alerts?walletId={{alert_wallet_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer1: malformed rule code -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED ("R9" is well formed and just matches nothing)
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/alerts?ruleCode=X1
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### customer1: alerts are for compliance officers only -> 403 ACCESS_DENIED
GET {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### NOT BUILT YET (SPEC §5, optional M15): AI-drafted case summary -> 403 today (no security rule, so denied)
POST {{aml}}/api/v1/aml/cases/{{fp_case_id}}/ai-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
